 video games are important when it  matters so you know something like Mass  Effect or twenty percent of The Walking  Dead is a more positive example of that  being implemented as long as we're on  the topic of negatives about this game  let's talk about the aesthetic and I  don't mean the graphics because those  are about serviceable for the time sure  the characters look a little stilted and  the facial animations could use some  work but otherwise it's fine what really  bugs me is just how ugly this game is  everything looks kind of disgusting like  this is one of the more unpleasant  looking games I can recall from recent  memory pretty much everything is either  covered in dust trash black slime mud or  some strange fluid that's a combination  of all of that the colors are so muted  and dull for a character that shoots  lightning which you think would be an  opening to make it have some really  bright and poppy neon colors but now the  aesthetic for the gameplay is  appropriate given the story they want to  tell since the city is in a state of  crisis it looks war-torn gross and  dangerous sure but sometimes it gets a  little hard to look at for hours and  hours on end and you'd like a break from  the glass shard filled mud being rubbed  in your eyes even fallout changed up the  aesthetic in certain areas just to give  you a break  save for the main menu screen we never  really get to see the city before it's a  Detroit hole so we can't exactly tell  how far it's fallen I think it would  have been more effective to see a  flashback of the city pretty explosion  or maybe just play a little bit prior to  Cole opening the bomb so we can get a  sense of progression for all we know  empire city has always looked like this  the gangs are just more active now maybe  I'm splitting hairs and that's a really  stupid complaint but it's something that  jumped out at me while replaying this  maybe as a kid I was more used to it  because a lot of games back then just  look like ugly brown and gray post  apocalypses even the spider-man games at  the time weren't very colorful at least  in this one they sometimes break up the  monotony of the visuals with these  motion comic style cutscenes that have  this kind of spray painted graffiti look  like runny splatter e ink all over the  place and very few colors with a grainy  texture to everything like it's all  painted on a brick wall I think this art  style is gritty like the gameplay but  stylized enough to also be visually  interesting instead of repugnant but the  cynic in me is still looking at them and  thinking boy they sure saved a lot of  money on animating  [Music]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  ten years later and one of the things  that still stuck with me the most was  how I hated the final morality choice  but also loved the ending of this game  so the villain who set all this stuff up  you know the guy running an evil  organization for decades that built the  superpower bomb  guiding you around to more moral  dilemmas and occasionally kicking your  ass he makes you make a choice between  saving 10 doctors or Cole's girlfriend  who kind of tolerates him again by this  point in the game whether you choose  true love or the needs of the many she  still dies I remember as a kid being  insanely frustrated when I picked the  group of doctors and got this death  scene and think to look up the other  option then because I was like 10 years  old so I rolled it back to an older save  file played like 40 minutes of the game  over again get back to this and chose  her instead only to get the same scene  your choice doesn't matter this was the  first time I ever experienced that in a  game so out of frustration from messing  up my hero run I went back again to get  the blue color version of the scene and  thinking I just couldn't trust this game  anymore it killed a lot of my hype for  the final hour of the game but then the  final boss made up for it and brought it  all back this bad guy Kesler has every  power you have plus all the other ones  you've seen in this game thus far from  the other enemies plus some new [ __ ] you  haven't seen any characters new and  reusing the blast zone as the final boss  arena was really cool as soon as this  fight started my hype levels rose again  because I had a bit of a hunch about the  ending that turned out to be true the  final boss is actually the player  character from the future my mind was  blown as a kid and I was so stoked that  I guessed it right based on all the  hints see old Cola here came from an  alternate future where he was a huge  coward who decided not to fight a super  villain that blew up the world and  killed his family so he went back in  time to train his younger self to be  less of a [ __ ] and make him strong  enough physically and emotionally to  fight that villain when it finally came  around and saved the world so in a sense  he's kind of still the good guy despite  being the bad guy I had never seen a  plot twist in a story like this up to  this point except for Benton race  against time  so this ending really won me back over  then BioShock Infinite ripped out  three years later and I audibly booed at  the screen it's not a perfect game by  any means because not every game can be  simpsons hit and run but it's got a lot  to talk about the gameplay isn't  anything innovative but it's very solid  and fun even to this day you really feel  like infamous the story is mostly  underwhelming but really pulls out all  the stops at the end overall I think I  found myself very attached to the  characters even though Zeke is basically  just Roman but like from Texas the  visual elements of it and a few of the  lame little gimmicks and signs of the  time haven't exactly aged well but they  don't hold the good parts back enough to  say it aged poorly overall the good  outshines the bad and I don't regret  replaying this at all I can even see  myself coming back to it again sometime  I don't say it's a groundbreaking  game-changer that define the genre nor  is it a mess beyond repair  nor will I say it's a beautiful love  letter to some oddly specific genre it's  simply just a solid game that's worth  playing if you like open-world superhero  junk and men with voices like sandpaper  just a quick reminder before you go that  I post my videos a day early on patreon  and give exclusive behind-the-scenes  content and patron exclusive videos  please consider becoming a patron it  really helps me out if you want a more  short-term way to support the channel  you can check out my merch and links in  the description we have t-shirts phone  cases posters mugs pillows baby onesies  and so much more see you next time  [Music]  [Music]
 

